WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.198
Zero Trust programs are
usually argued by citation,

2
00:00:03.198 --> 00:00:06.200
and most of the citations
fail when you check them.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.863
Four documents get cited
as if they were one.

4
00:00:08.863 --> 00:00:11.645
Executive Order 14028 is binding,

5
00:00:11.645 --> 00:00:16.713
and required each agency to plan
for Zero Trust Architecture.

6
00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:21.987
OMB M-22-09 is binding, and sets
specific actions by pillar.

7
00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:25.963
CISA's maturity model is guidance;
it says it shouldn't be viewed

8
00:00:25.963 --> 00:00:30.088
as a strict set of requirements,
and its page is now marked archived.

9
00:00:30.088 --> 00:00:34.237
NIST SP 800-207 is guidance too.

10
00:00:34.237 --> 00:00:38.739
M-22-09 borrows the model's
pillars to organize its actions,

11
00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:41.562
but doesn't adopt its
stages as requirements.

12
00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:45.250
That leaves several requirements
that circulate but don't exist.

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.862
No federal document requires a particular
maturity stage, such as Advanced.

14
00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:53.026
No federal document
defines a Zero Trust score,

15
00:00:53.026 --> 00:00:58.462
so a tool that claims to certify maturity
is citing a requirement that isn't there.

16
00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:04.887
And M-22-09 doesn't require
ScubaGear; that comes from BOD 25-01.

17
00:01:04.887 --> 00:01:06.788
None of that makes the target vague.

18
00:01:06.788 --> 00:01:10.962
It means the target is a choice
the agency makes and has to defend.

19
00:01:10.962 --> 00:01:14.600
So the decision: set a maturity
target for each pillar,

20
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.575
written down as program
design, not mandate.

21
00:01:17.575 --> 00:01:21.368
The Zero Trust program lead
decides it, consulting the CIO,

22
00:01:21.368 --> 00:01:26.425
the CISO and the authorizing official,
before the next assessment is scored.

23
00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:29.140
Next, the one memo that still binds.
